{"id":"mahabharata-7-094","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":94,"title":"चतुर्नवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 94 · Satyaki kills Sudarshana","summary":{"en":"Having passed Drona, Satyaki fights and kills the Kamboja king's son Sudarshana in a mighty duel. The warriors on both sides praise his feat as he goes on.","kn":"ದ್ರೋಣನನ್ನು ದಾಟಿದ ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಕಾಂಬೋಜ ರಾಜನ ಮಗ ಸುದರ್ಶನನನ್ನು ಭೀಕರ ದ್ವಂದ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನು ಮುಂದುವರಿದಂತೆ ಎರಡೂ ಕಡೆಯ ವೀರರು ಅವನ ಸಾಹಸವನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"द्रोण को पार कर सात्यकि भीषण द्वन्द्व में काम्बोज राजा के पुत्र सुदर्शन को मार देता है। आगे बढ़ते हुए दोनों पक्षों के योद्धा उसके पराक्रम की प्रशंसा करते हैं।","te":"ద్రోణుని దాటిన సాత్యకి కాంభోజ రాజు కుమారుడు సుదర్శనుని భీకర ద్వంద్వంలో చంపుతాడు. అతడు సాగుతుండగా ఇరుపక్షాల వీరులు అతని పరాక్రమాన్ని కొనియాడతారు.","ta":"த்ரோணரைக் கடந்த சாத்யகி கொடிய தனிப்போரில் காம்போஜ மன்னனின் மகன் சுதர்சனனைக் கொல்கிறான். அவன் முன்னேறுகையில் இரு தரப்பு வீரர்களும் அவன் வீரத்தைப் புகழ்கின்றனர்.","ml":"ദ്രോണരെ കടന്നശേഷം സാത്യകി കംബോജരാജാവിന്റെ പുത്രൻ സുദർശനനെ കഠിനമായ ദ്വന്ദ്വയുദ്ധത്തിൽ പൊരുതി വധിക്കുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ഈ നേട്ടത്തെ ഇരുപക്ഷത്തെയും യോദ്ധാക്കൾ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.94; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"द्रोणं स जित्वा पुरुषप्रवीर-\nस्तथैव हार्दिक्यमुखांस्त्वदीयान् ।\nप्रहस्य सूतं वचनं बभाषे\nशिनिप्रवीरः कुरुपुंगवाग्र्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having conquered Drona, that hero among men, and likewise your men led by Hridika's son, the heroic Shini, laughing, spoke to his charioteer, O foremost of the Kuru bulls."}},{"n":2,"text":"निमित्तमात्रं वयमत्र सूत\nदग्धारयः केशवफल्गुनाभ्याम् ।\nहतान्निहन्मेह नरर्षभेण\nवयं सुरेशात्मसमुद्भवेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We are only the instrument here, charioteer. The enemies were burned by Keshava and Phalguna; I kill here those already killed by that bull among men, born of Indra's own self.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"तमेवमुक्त्वा शिनिपुंगवस्तदा\nमहामृधे सोऽग्र्यधनुर्धरोऽरिहा ।\nकिरन्समन्तात्सहसा शरान्बली\nसमापतच्छ्येन इवामिषं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having so spoken to him, the bull of the Shinis, strong, the foremost bowman, slayer of foes, in that great battle scattering arrows on all sides, swooped suddenly like a falcon on meat."}},{"n":4,"text":"तं यान्तमश्वैः शशिशङ्खवर्णै-\nर्विगाह्य सैन्यं पुरुषप्रवीरम् ।\nनाशक्नुवन्वारयितुं समन्ता-\nदादित्यरश्मिप्रतिमं नराग्र्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he went on with his moon-and-conch-white horses, having plunged into the army, none could stop that hero, the best of men, who was like a ray of the sun."}},{"n":5,"text":"असह्यविक्रान्तमदीनसत्त्वं\nसर्वे गणा भारत दुर्विषह्यम् ।\nसहस्रनेत्रप्रतिमप्रभावं\nदिवीव सूर्यं जलदव्यपाये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Every host, O Bharata, found him hard to endure, unbearable in valor, undaunted in spirit, like the thousand-eyed Indra in power, like the sun in the sky when the clouds have gone."}},{"n":6,"text":"अमर्षपूर्णस्त्वतिचित्रयोधी\nशरासनी काञ्चनवर्मधारी ।\nसुदर्शनः सात्यकिमापतन्तं\nन्यवारयद्राजवरः प्रसह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filled with anger, a most varied fighter, with a bow and golden armor, the noble Sudarshana forcibly checked Satyaki as he advanced."}},{"n":7,"text":"तयोरभूद्भरत संप्रहारः\nसुदारुणस्तं समभिप्रशंसन् ।\nयोधास्त्वदीयाश्च हि सोमकाश्च\nवृत्रेन्द्रयोर्युद्धमिवामरौघाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A very dreadful clash took place between them, O Bharata, which your warriors and the Somakas praised, like the fight of Vritra and Indra watched by throngs of immortals."}},{"n":8,"text":"शरैः सुतीक्ष्णैः शतशोऽभ्यविध्य-\nत्सुदर्शनः सात्वतमुख्यमाजौ ।\nअनागतानेव तु तान्पृषत्कां-\nश्चिच्छेद बाणैः शिनिपुंगवोऽपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sudarshana struck the foremost Satvata in the battle with hundreds of very sharp arrows, but the bull of the Shinis cut those shafts before they arrived."}},{"n":9,"text":"तथैव शक्रप्रतिमोऽपि सात्यकिः\nसुदर्शने यान्क्षिपति स्म सायकान् ।\nद्विधा त्रिधा तानकरोत्सुदर्शनः\nशरोत्तमैः स्यन्दनवर्यमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise, Satyaki, like Indra, whatever arrows he shot at Sudarshana, Sudarshana, standing in his excellent chariot, cut into two or three with his best arrows."}},{"n":10,"text":"संप्रेक्ष्य बाणान्निहतांस्तदानीं\nसुदर्शनः सात्यकिबाणवेगैः ।\nक्रोधाद्दिधक्षन्निव तिग्मतेजाः\nशरानमुञ्चत्तपनीयचित्रान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his arrows destroyed by the speed of Satyaki's shafts, Sudarshana, of keen splendor, as though wishing to burn him in anger, shot arrows bright with gold."}},{"n":11,"text":"पुनः स बाणैस्त्रिभिरग्निकल्पै-\nराकर्णपूर्णैर्निशितैः सुपुङ्खैः ।\nविव्याध देहावरणं विभिद्य\nते सात्यकेराविविशुः शरीरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again with three sharp, fine-feathered arrows, like fires, drawn to the ear, he struck Satyaki, breaking his armor, and they entered his body."}},{"n":12,"text":"तथैव तस्यावनिपालपुत्रः\nसंधाय बाणैरपरैर्ज्वलद्भिः ।\nआजघ्निवांस्तान्रजतप्रकाशां-\nश्चतुर्भिरश्वांश्चतुरः प्रसह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the prince, fixing other blazing arrows, forcibly struck the four silvery horses with four."}},{"n":13,"text":"तथा तु तेनाभिहतस्तरस्वी\nनप्ता शिनेरिन्द्रसमानवीर्यः ।\nसुदर्शनस्येषुगणैः सुतीक्ष्णै-\nर्हयान्निहत्याशु ननाद नादम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck thus by him, the mighty grandson of Shini, equal to Indra in valor, killed Sudarshana's horses with his keen volleys and quickly roared."}},{"n":14,"text":"अथास्य सूतस्य शिरो निकृत्य\nभल्लेन वज्राशनिसंनिभेन ।\nसुदर्शनस्यापि शिनिप्रवीरः\nक्षुरेण चिच्छेद शिरः प्रसह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, cutting off the head of his charioteer with a broad-headed arrow like Indra's thunderbolt, the Shini hero forcibly cut off Sudarshana's head too with a razor-headed arrow."}},{"n":15,"text":"सकुण्डलं पूर्णशशिप्रकाशं\nभ्राजिष्णु वक्त्रं निचकर्त देहात् ।\nयथा पुरा वज्रधरः प्रसह्य\nबलस्य संख्येऽतिबलस्य राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cut from the body the shining face, with earrings, radiant as the full moon, as the wielder of the thunderbolt once forcibly cut off Bala, the mighty, in battle, O king."}},{"n":16,"text":"निहत्य तं पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रं\nरणे यदूनामृषभस्तरस्वी ।\nमुदा समेतः परया महात्मा\nरराज राजन्सुरराजकल्पः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having slain that prince, the grandson of a king, in battle, the mighty bull of the Yadus, the great-souled one, joined with supreme joy, shone, O king, like the king of the gods."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततो ययावर्जुनमेव येन\nनिवार्य सैन्यं तव मार्गणौघैः ।\nसदश्वयुक्तेन रथेन निर्या-\nल्लोकान्विसिस्मापयिषुर्नृवीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he went on toward Arjuna, checking your army with his volleys of arrows, speeding in his chariot with its fine horses, wishing to astonish the worlds."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्तस्य विस्मापयनीयमग्र्य-\nमपूजयन्योधवराः समेताः ।\nयद्वर्तमानानिषुगोचरेऽरी-\nन्ददाह बाणैर्हुतभुग्यथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The assembled best warriors praised that excellent and astonishing feat of his, that he burned the enemies within range of his arrows with his shafts as fire burns."}}]}]}